<title>USA: FGIC qualifies four issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>FGIC qualifies four issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Guaranty Insurance Co on Monday said that it qualified four municipal bond issues, which will be sold competitively, for insurance.</p>
<p>--New Haven Unified School District, Calif., $14 million General Obligations.</p>
<p>--Mohawk School District, N.Y., $9 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Oklahoma City, Okla., $47.5 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Highland Village, Texas, $4.090 million Tax and Revenues.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650)).</p>
</text>
